---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
const lastUpdated = "August 18, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Covey collects, uses, and protects information across the app and website."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-[var(--section-y)]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Privacy</div>
    <h1 class="display t-h1 mb-4">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-ink-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] mb-12">
      Last updated {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <div class="card p-6 mb-12">
      <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-ink">Scope of this page:</strong> this policy is a
        plain-language draft for Covey's product app and {SITE.domain}
        marketing website. It covers account data, plans, messages, location,
        analytics, payments, support requests, and deletion choices.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed text-lg">
      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Covey collects information you give us, such as your name, email
          address, profile details, city, support messages, waitlist details,
          and anything you choose to add to a plan, recap, comment, or message.
          If you create an account, we also receive account identifiers from
          our authentication provider.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The app may process plan details, attendance, saved places,
          bookmarks, chat messages, photos or media you upload, and approximate
          or precise location when you choose to use location-based features.
          Payment details are handled by Stripe; Covey does not store full card
          numbers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          We use this information to run Covey, create and show plans, deliver
          messages, personalize recommendations, process payments, send service
          updates, respond to support requests, investigate safety reports, and
          understand whether the product is working. We use website and product
          analytics to improve onboarding, performance, and reliability.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We do not sell your personal information. We do not use private
          messages or non-public plan content for third-party advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Who processes it</h2>
        <p>
          Covey uses service providers to operate the app and website. These
          include Supabase for authentication, database, storage, and backend
          infrastructure; Stripe for payments; hosting providers for the
          website and app; and analytics or error-reporting tools that help us
          understand usage and diagnose problems. These providers process data
          for Covey so we can provide the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Location and visibility</h2>
        <p>
          Location features are meant to help people discover plans and places.
          You can control device location permissions through your operating
          system. Some plan, profile, and activity information may be visible to
          other people depending on the feature, your relationship to those
          people, and the privacy settings available in the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Deletion and choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to access, correct, export, or delete information tied
          to your account. Account deletion is available from the app when
          signed in; you can also contact support if you need help. Deletion may
          not remove information we must keep for security, fraud prevention,
          payment records, legal obligations, backups, or abuse investigations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy:
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.support}`} class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">
            {SITE.emails.support}
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
